== 3. What 39b needs =========================================== 
  1. the file and column holding TOTAL burden (TMB), and whether it 
     is a raw count or already per-megabase 
  2. the columns holding SBS7a/b/c/d, so UV burden and the UV 
     FRACTION can be derived rather than assumed 
  3. whether a NON-UV burden (TMB minus SBS7) can be computed, which 
     is the cleanest way to separate a UV-specific effect from a 
     general mutation-load effect 
  4. the purity column, without which the central confound cannot be 
     tested 
  5. the identifier to join on, and how many samples survive 
 
  PRE-SPECIFICATION, recorded now, before any association is computed: 
    PRIMARY   Spearman correlation of RASSF9 expression with TOTAL 
              mutational burden, in the largest cohort with both. 
    FAMILY    total burden, UV (SBS7) burden, non-UV burden, UV 
              fraction -- four definitions x two genes = 8 tests, 
              Benjamini-Hochberg corrected across the family. Every 
              one is reported whatever it shows. 
    CONFOUND  the association must survive adjustment for purity and 
              sample type, and the premises of the purity explanation 
              are tested individually as they were for methylation. 
    ROBUSTNESS Spearman alongside Pearson on log burden, since the 
              original analysis found rho = -0.130 (p = 0.021) while 
              r = -0.033 (p = 0.564) -- a gap that usually means a 
              few extreme-burden tumours drive the rank result. 
    NOT CLAIMABLE Cross-sectional bulk data cannot establish that 
              burden causes repression, nor the direction of any 
              arrow. 39b will report association only. 
